{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:04PW:proof", "parent_tag": "04PV", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "The affine case of the bijection is\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nFor general schemes <MATH_0001> the bijection follows by covering <MATH_0002> by affines\nand glueing. Details omitted. For the final assertion, observe that the\nprojection <MATH_0003> is a flat\n(Lemma <REF_0002>) closed immersion which\nis bijective on underlying topological spaces and hence must be\nan isomorphism by the bijection established in the first part of the proof.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-pure-open-closed-specializations}", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$Z \\times_{X, g} Y \\to Y$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-flat}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:bb846b93029b1f1e9a5f2b9e444477a9d53162b701c5698b265683928a6bc14c", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:baf819cb9cdbb771066ac529ef944fc79c99da4331b9b58f297019db759822cf", "source_math_hash": "sha256:10bef30ad6ff1c14148dd21290a9b3427c3c5430a78a791f3dd3d499131b2a7c"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:0819:statement", "parent_tag": "04PV", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "A flat closed immersion of finite presentation\nis the open immersion of an open and closed subscheme.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-flat-closed-immersions-finite-presentation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:df7c81cac16bb511ab4ad7c089bc7d33e066570397cce4d7c3e5f97e104aa382", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ca69d3dd56a5261e7fd152ffc3ed670640f951316a83cf953e1ce392261ad298", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:0819:proof", "parent_tag": "04PV", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "The affine case is\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nIn general the lemma follows by covering <MATH_0001> by affines.\nDetails omitted.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-finitely-generated-pure-ideal}", "MATH_0001": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:46287a5073387baa42cc5fdb8e46c5d16657c899e99e5375c2c2b1d759edcb2c", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a81f8d80fe13af3a994ea0cba743cbc8781b68f877af3fc58377ec22260cc06a", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d2cdd54c91172842da7935e351b2e537dfc65808da525fec53dd82898c278104"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:04PV:prose-0002", "parent_tag": "04PV", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that a connected component <MATH_0001> of a scheme <MATH_0002> is a closed\nsubset stable under generalization. Hence the following definition\nmakes sense.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:cb0c7ad64014dbb3512a87919c84874c2368fb008adeb17f42ef4cbf6d5cdb42", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3511e79726620baa1d5a1c27bb00a753527ba5f2465076f06a1a5871c135bdf9", "source_math_hash": "sha256:75f5511e4eeb503a751e4ea5a606b0eed23babafc596b0871ad110c4f4ecb8f7"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:04PX:statement", "parent_tag": "04PV", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a connected component.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>canonical scheme structure on <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is the unique\nscheme structure on <MATH_0004> such that the closed immersion <MATH_0005>\nis flat, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$T \\subset X$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$T \\to X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-flat-closed-immersions}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-scheme-structure-connected-component}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:c19769e75538c47d90358ccd4fa6459b3b4d70ec252934c7a1e12a299f36ecbf", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d87ef4a06b8c51209bc8be60c59fbc8d368560f839094162762f4d158b64ddc2", "source_math_hash": "sha256:990360944ae6aa3c4bcbb2ab5bfd7472e2a6324d24a43efe2d48e1cf7c99a9c4"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:04PV:prose-0003", "parent_tag": "04PV", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt turns out that we can determine when every finite flat\n<MATH_0001>-module is finite locally free using the previous lemma.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:c9943d71a91bcf3a6b7f5de685a73d5aeffb258beb4089474cba73e56d90ab20", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fe2c0ead510bb863ac1c9521cd37581c9dc95873949623e32e1aa7b3eecf68d8", "source_math_hash": "sha256:08df7f0582f62c0bc7633498f6928e80e8596b3646363534c509b5fe368b727e"}
